    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d720">

                <pb facs="0756" n="644" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg644"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.48/915: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cole</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Archangel</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-08-02T18:00:00+04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 2, 1919,
                                6 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received August 3, 3:55
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>1358. Department’s telegram number 717, July 22 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >23</hi>], 4 p.m. For reasons given in my 1357, August 2, 5 p.m.<anchor n="46"
                        xml:id="d720-f1"/> steamer <hi rendition="#italic">Redondo</hi> should not
                    proceed to Archangel. The British have sent flour which is now here and are
                    sending more which will suffice until evacuation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Cole</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d720-f1" n="46" xml:id="d720-f1-content">
                <p>Transmitted in telegram from the Ambassador in Great Britain, no. 2687, Aug. 3,
                        <hi rendition="#italic">infra.</hi></p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
